Fall back to sinf/cosf on Apple platforms.

harfbuzz's meson probes for `sincosf` with cc.has_function(), which succeeds
because the symbol is present in libSystem, and then defines HAVE_SINCOSF. But
Apple's math.h never declares `sincosf` (it spells it `__sincosf`), so the call
below fails to compile with "use of undeclared identifier". Taking the
sinf/cosf path instead is behaviourally identical; it costs one extra
transcendental in variable composite glyph rendering, which is not a path video
playback touches at all.

--- a/src/OT/glyf/VarCompositeGlyph.hh
+++ b/src/OT/glyf/VarCompositeGlyph.hh
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@
     rotation = rotation * HB_PI;
     float c;
     float s;
-#ifdef HAVE_SINCOSF
+#if defined(HAVE_SINCOSF) && !defined(__APPLE__)
     sincosf (rotation, &s, &c);
 #else
     c = cosf (rotation);
